<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="4f4dda2c">&lt;p&gt;
    To track and receive communication and events feedback, the practitioner should:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Request, receive and analyze feedback from the target audience through the pre-established feedback mechanism
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Identify appropriate actions to address feedback (if required)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Inform those who provided feedback with an update that addresses their questions, concerns, and ideas
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    It is important to conduct on-going evaluation of communication needs, which can be accomplished through the following:
    &amp;nbsp;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Identify pros and cons of each stakeholder engagement channel against effectiveness and impact, and feed into the
        communications plan (as required)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Prioritize engagement channels to be used and develop effective communication collateral to deploy on-going and
        targeted engagement
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Identify communications and events channels that need to be paused, stopped or continued
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Identify additional communication channels (if required)
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
